    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan recommends a Hold, and the evidence supports this balanced conclusion. JPM is at its 60-day peak with price above all major moving averages in bullish alignment, supported by a fortress balance sheet ($3.88T assets, $327.9B equity, $13B operating cash flow). However, RSI at 72.92 is overbought, price is 26.7% above the 200-day SMA (statistically extreme), and bearish divergence is present (lower RSI and MACD histogram peaks despite higher price highs). The income statement is not in the supplied evidence, and sentiment/news/macro data are unavailable, creating a genuine data vacuum. Near-term risk/reward is unfavorable (only ~0.5% upside to upper Bollinger Band vs ~8.8% downside to 50 SMA), so I will not add new exposure at $190.06. Existing holders should maintain positions with a trailing stop below the 10-day EMA at $185.94 and reduce by half on a break below the 20-day SMA at $182.31. Reassess after Q1 2024 earnings.\n\n**Stop Loss**: 185.94\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain target weight; do not add new exposure at current levels. For existing holders, keep position size at target weight with trailing stop below 10-day EMA ($185.94).\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
